The instantaneous voltage across the inductor is expressed as the product of inductance and rate of change of current through it.

{V_L} = Lfrac{{di}}{{dt}}

Power is expressed as the product of current and voltage.

P = {V_L}i = Lifrac{{di}}{{dt}}

Hence instantaneous power in an inductor is proportional to the product of instantaneous current and rate of change of current through it.
